@ Logical, and, or, not, truth, falsity, implies

.. Conjunction, disjunction, negation, and implication.
.. truth and falsity are the constants, because true and false are keywords.
& Logical a
  .. Conjunction.
  and ( a a -- a )
  .. Disjunction.
  or ( a a -- a )
  .. The opposite value.
  not ( a -- a )
  .. The constant that and leaves unchanged.
  truth ( -- a )
  .. The constant that or leaves unchanged.
  falsity ( -- a )

.. The lower value implies the upper one.
: implies ( Logical a => a a -- a )
  swap not swap or

. ..................................................................................................

# Logical Bool
  and = and_bool
  or = or_bool
  not = not_bool
  truth = truth_bool
  falsity = falsity_bool

: foreign and_bool ( Bool Bool -- Bool )
: foreign or_bool ( Bool Bool -- Bool )
: foreign not_bool ( Bool -- Bool )

: truth_bool ( -- Bool )
  true

: falsity_bool ( -- Bool )
  false
